WEBVTT

00:00:00.433 --> 00:00:02.467
Are you a SMART fella...

00:00:02.467 --> 00:00:04.533
or a FART smella?

00:00:04.533 --> 00:00:06.800
Let's find OUT!

00:00:07.700 --> 00:00:10.433
Question six, a word analogy!

00:00:10.433 --> 00:00:11.833
Ocean is to puddle,

00:00:11.833 --> 00:00:13.733
as mountain is to...

00:00:13.733 --> 00:00:16.167
what? A, valley...

00:00:16.333 --> 00:00:18.567
B, hill... C,

00:00:18.567 --> 00:00:20.200
river... or D,

00:00:20.200 --> 00:00:22.433
rock? Five seconds!

00:00:27.933 --> 00:00:30.467
TIME'S UP! Pencils down!

00:00:30.833 --> 00:00:33.467
It's... B, hill!

00:00:33.467 --> 00:00:35.300
An ocean shrinks down to a

00:00:35.300 --> 00:00:37.633
tiny puddle, so a mountain shrinks

00:00:37.633 --> 00:00:39.367
down to a little hill.

00:00:39.367 --> 00:00:41.867
Same thing, pocket-sized!

00:00:42.800 --> 00:00:45.800
Question thirteen, a picture puzzle!

00:00:45.800 --> 00:00:48.067
A dot marches clockwise around

00:00:48.067 --> 00:00:49.933
a square: top-left,

00:00:49.933 --> 00:00:52.167
top-right, bottom-right... where

00:00:52.167 --> 00:00:53.833
does it jump next?

00:00:53.933 --> 00:00:56.267
A, top-left... B,

00:00:56.267 --> 00:00:59.200
bottom-left... C, top-right...

00:00:59.200 --> 00:01:01.033
or D, the center?

00:01:01.033 --> 00:01:02.800
Five seconds!

00:01:08.333 --> 00:01:10.867
TIME'S UP! Pencils down!

00:01:11.167 --> 00:01:12.533
The answer is...

00:01:12.533 --> 00:01:16.067
B, bottom-left! The dot steps clockwise,

00:01:16.067 --> 00:01:17.133
corner to corner,

00:01:17.133 --> 00:01:18.800
and right after bottom-right,

00:01:18.800 --> 00:01:21.200
the next corner is bottom-left!

00:01:22.067 --> 00:01:25.033
Question fourteen, a number analogy!

00:01:25.033 --> 00:01:26.167
Two makes five,

00:01:26.167 --> 00:01:27.367
three makes seven,

00:01:27.367 --> 00:01:28.633
four makes nine,

00:01:28.633 --> 00:01:30.167
so five makes...

00:01:30.167 --> 00:01:32.000
what? A, ten...

00:01:32.000 --> 00:01:33.967
B, eleven... C,

00:01:33.967 --> 00:01:35.600
twelve... or D,

00:01:35.600 --> 00:01:37.967
thirteen? Five seconds!

00:01:43.467 --> 00:01:46.000
TIME'S UP! Pencils down!

00:01:46.400 --> 00:01:48.833
It's... B, eleven!

00:01:48.833 --> 00:01:50.300
Each number is doubled,

00:01:50.300 --> 00:01:51.733
then add one.

00:01:51.733 --> 00:01:53.733
Five times two is ten,

00:01:53.733 --> 00:01:56.033
plus one is eleven!

00:01:57.200 --> 00:02:00.133
So, are you smart or fart?

00:02:00.133 --> 00:02:01.900
Count up your correct answers to

00:02:01.900 --> 00:02:03.533
find your rank!

00:02:04.467 --> 00:02:05.967
So, how did you do?

00:02:05.967 --> 00:02:07.400
Comment your score below,

00:02:07.400 --> 00:02:09.067
and follow for more!
